---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="My Kenresoft CMS site">
  <h1>It's working!</h1>
  <p>
    This page isn't fetching anything from your CMS yet — see
    <code>src/pages/blog/index.astro</code> and <code>src/pages/blog/[slug].astro</code> for a
    working example, and <code>src/lib/cms.ts</code> for the client itself.
  </p>
  <p>
    Set <code>PUBLIC_KENRESOFT_CMS_URL</code> in <code>.env</code> to your deployed API Worker's
    URL (or <code>http://localhost:8787</code> while running the CMS locally), then adjust the
    <code>contentType</code> string in the blog example to match a real content type in your own
    deployment — <code>'blog-post'</code> here is just a placeholder name.
  </p>
</Layout>
